# OrcaRouter variant: Qwen3.8-27B Uncensored NVFP4 (abliterated) on the NInfer
# fork. Published by igorls; see the README's OrcaRouter section for provenance,
# checksums and the limits of the vendor's qualification.
#
# Profile mirrors the default variant: MTP3, the full 262K window, preserved
# thinking. Three things differ, all forced by the artifact or the fork engine:
#   * KV_DTYPE=nvfp4 - at 262K an fp8 pool alone needs 9.66 GiB and the 26 GB
#     artifact leaves 8.77 GiB after weights; k8v4 misses by ~2 MB, nvfp4 fits.
#   * KV_CAPACITY explicit and MAX_CONCURRENCY=2 - fork revision 91ce2f2c dies
#     with "fatal executor failure (St11logic_error: isolated-feasible request
#     is blocked in an idle Engine)" whenever the pool does not exactly back the
#     configured lanes: observed at C=4 with the auto pool (5,293 page groups)
#     and at C=4 with an explicit 262,144-token pool. Two lanes with a pool of
#     exactly one full-context sequence survived the reproduction
#     (bench_tagged.py: a 70K prefill then a distinct 72K generation) three
#     times. Do not add --clamp-concurrency-to-pool: it fails startup with
#     "Main KV page count N is outside the target capacity curve".
#   * --desktop-reserve-gib 0 and --prefill-chunk 2048 - fork-only flags (this
#     revision reserves an 8 GiB desktop floor by default, which cannot fit).
#
# Engine: igorls/ninfer @ 91ce2f2c — the artifact manifest's minimum_revision.
# That revision is MSVC-only in part, so run.sh applies
# patches/orcarouter/0001-linux-build-portability.patch after staging, and the
# build uses CUDA 13.3.1 (the revision's qualified toolkit) because its
# Flash-Next target needs the CCCL header only 13.3 ships.
NINFER_SRC=../ninfer-orcarouter
SRC_DIR=ninfer-src-orcarouter
CUDA_VERSION=13.3.1

IMAGE_TAG=ninfer-qwen38-27b-orcarouter-nvfp4:latest
CONTAINER_NAME=ninfer-orcarouter
COMPOSE_PROJECT=qwen38-27b-orcarouter-nvfp4-ninfer
# Same port and same model alias as the default variant: agents keep one profile
# and only one variant runs at a time (`run.sh up` stops the other one).
HOST_PORT=8080

MODEL_FILE=/models/orcarouter/qwen3_8_27b_orcarouter_nvfp4.ninfer
MODEL_ID=qwen3.8-27b

MAX_CONTEXT=262144
KV_CAPACITY=262144
MAX_CONCURRENCY=2
KV_DTYPE=nvfp4
EXTRA_ARGS="--desktop-reserve-gib 0 --prefill-chunk 2048 --device-state-slots 2 --host-state-slots 8 --host-kv-mib 8192 --spec mtp --draft-tokens 3 --lm-head-draft --preserve-thinking"
